<misterromdescription>
    <name>Rim Rockin' Basketball (v2.0)</name>
    <setname>rimrockn20</setname>
    <rbf>Gm0rk_ITech8</rbf>
    <mameversion>0289</mameversion>
    <mratimestamp>20261010</mratimestamp>
    <year>1991</year>
    <manufacturer>Strata / Incredible Technologies</manufacturer>
    <category>Sports / Basketball</category>
    <players>4</players>
    <joystick>8-way</joystick>
    <rotation>horizontal</rotation>
    <num_buttons>2</num_buttons>
    <buttons names="Shoot,Pass,Start,Coin,Service" default="A,B,Start,R,L"/>

    <romstruct>
Board select (ioctl index 1): 03 = itech8 6809 board (3); second byte 32 =
2 page large display at 8 MHz (bits 2-1 = 1), YM3812 sound board with a VIA
(bits 4-3 = 2), Rim Rockin' Basketball's board (bit 5: 3 MHz CPU, bank
register at $01A0, 128 KB program, ports $0161-$0165); third byte 09 =
Rim Rockin' Basketball's inputs (four players).
Download stream (ioctl index 0), 1,474,560 bytes:
000000 - 007FFF   32K  sound program                  -> block RAM
008000 - 027FFF  128K  main program                   -> SDRAM bank 0
028000 - 067FFF  256K  OKI samples                    -> SDRAM bank 2
068000 - 167FFF    1M  graphics ROMs                  -> SDRAM bank 1
    </romstruct>

    <rom index="1">
        <part>03 32 09</part>
    </rom>

    <rom index="0" zip="rimrockn20.zip|rimrockn.zip" md5="7be2139d8108e6e8b21c7de183c7bdaf">
        <!-- sound program (sound CPU $8000-$FFFF) -->
        <part name="rrbsnd_v1.1_u27.u27" crc="59f87f0e"/>
        <!-- main program (128 KB: banks 0-3 of its first 64 KB at $4000, last 32 KB at $8000) -->
        <part name="rrb.bim_2.0_u5.u5" crc="7e9d5545"/>
        <!-- OKI M6295 samples -->
        <part name="rbb-srom0" crc="7ad42be0"/>
        <!-- graphics ROMs -->
        <part name="rbb-grom00" crc="3eacbad9"/>
        <part name="rbb-grom01" crc="864cc269"/>
        <part name="rbb-grom02-2" crc="47904233"/>
        <part name="rbb-grom03-2" crc="f005f118"/>
    </rom>

    <!-- 8 KB battery-backed RAM (CPU $2000-$3FFF) -->
    <nvram index="4" size="8192"/>
</misterromdescription>
